A||||3||artherd||Ever LIFT the inside front wheel in a corner under power?||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||11-24-2001||08:22 PM||||Just came back from a 'sorting' run to our 'proving grounds' or so we call them. Curvy little ~1mile section of extreme twisties that also climbs about 800feet <P>The car is handling great, I think we've really hit it with these new alignment settings... one hard right-handed up-hill curve, the car will LIFT THE INSIDE WHEEL, then a fraction of a second later, as the car crests the same hill, I actually get some very brief wheelspin... in 2nd gear.. SECOND! ... (this is a stock 2.8 motor, and fairly grippy dunlop 215/45/17 front, 235/40/17 rear tyres, it won't spin at all in first when the clutch is dumped at 3,500+rpm... just *GOES*...)<P>We need a Gtech, or a better accelerometer. But I'm convinced we're now well over 1G.<P>And the car is totally neutural, drift, over or understeer selectable quite easily with the throttle, at any point. Watch the rear-end though, when it goes, you have to CATCH it ;0)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>Now I've just gotta make it pull as hard in 4th as it does in first....<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||Nashco||11-24-2001||08:38 PM||||So, what're the new alignment specs??<P>What do you have for suspension?  I'll automatically assume poly all around, lowering springs..coil overs or no?  More info!!! LOL<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||MrPBody||11-24-2001||09:48 PM||||I have seen old 911's and Alfa GTV's lift the inside front wheel, usually at Road Atlanta's Turn 3.  Sounds like serious front roll stiffness.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||11-25-2001||03:43 AM||||Whoopsies.<P>Front:<BR>-1.5degree camber<BR>stock caster.<BR>1/8" toe OUT.<P>Rear -1 camber<BR>1/16" toe OUT.<P>This is where the car seems to turn the hardest, yet still be streetable for daily driving (probally will wear the tyres a little fast, and I wouldn't take it above 100mph anymore. at least not with that rear toe out.)<P>Car has poly everything, front springs cut exactly one coil, stock height rears, and Konis. (got a *cheap* good used set)  Stock (large, 88) bars! (new endlinks, new everything infact.)  Pretty simple slightly-better-than stock suspension, and a set of grippy 17"s.  Our cars have *amazing* potential!<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">     <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 11-25-2001).]||||reg||3
